@startuml 04-activity-ngo-registration
' Activity Diagram - NGO Registration and Verification
' The second activity diagram, covering the trust workflow that the whole
' platform rests on. Mirrors the reference "manage hairstylists" figure in
' shape: a decision that branches into distinct maintenance paths.
!include common.puml

|NGO|
start
:Open NGO registration form;
:Enter organisation details\n(name, PAN, registration no.,\nDarpan ID, address);
:Upload Registration Certificate\nand PAN Card;

|SYSTEM|
:Receive uploaded documents;

if (Document has a text layer?) then ([yes])
  :Extract text using\nApache PDFBox;
else ([no - scanned image])
  :Extract text using\nTesseract OCR;
endif

:Match text against keywords\nexpected for the document type;

if (Verification result?) then ([UNREADABLE])
  :Flag document as UNREADABLE;
elseif (   ) then ([keywords missing])
  :Flag document as\nLOOKS_SUSPICIOUS;
else ([keywords found])
  :Cross-check declared PAN and\nregistration number against text;
  :Flag document as LOOKS_VALID;
endif

:Upload documents to Cloudinary\nas private resources;
:Save NGO with status PENDING;
:Withhold NGO from all\npublic listings;

|ADMINISTRATOR|
:Open pending applications queue;
:View documents through\ntime-limited signed URL;
:Review automated\nverification flags;

if (Decision?) then ([Reject])
  |SYSTEM|
  :Set status REJECTED\nand record reason;
  |NGO|
  :Receive rejection\nwith reason;
  stop
else ([Approve])
endif

|SYSTEM|
:Set status APPROVED;
:Generate unique NGO identifier;
:Create zero NGO balance record;
:Publish NGO to public listings;

|NGO|
:Sign in and manage profile,\nevents, needs and finances;

stop

@enduml
